d  but Phaeton now to have MV put a stop to  it by opposing me in the Midway with his  hippo my army seized we were overcome  and assisted our forces at that time  being unequal to theirs I have now  however resolved to renew the war and  fix my colony if you have a mind you  shall accompany us in the expedition  I will furnish you every one with a  royal vulture and other accoutrements we  shall set out tomorrow with all my heart  said I whenever you please we stayed  however and supped with him and rising  early the next day preceded with the  army when the spies gave us notice that  the enemy was approaching the army  consisted of a hundred thousand  besides the scouts and the engineers  together with the auxiliaries amongst  them were 80,000 hipa gippy and twenty  thousand who were mounted on the latch  and op Terry  these are very large birds whose  feathers are a kind of herb and whose  wings look like lettuces next to these  stood the sintra Bali and thus Garuda  Maquis  our allies from the north were three  thousand select occitane and five  thousand and nama Johnny the former take  their names from the fleas which they  ride upon every flea being as big as  twelve elephants the latter our foot  soldiers and are carried about in the  air without wings in this manner they  have large gowns hanging down to their  feet these they tuck up and spread in  the form of a sail and the wind drives  them about like so many boats in the  battle they generally wear targets it  was reported that 70,000 strata belani  from the stars over cappadocia was said  to be there together with 5000 hipa  Gorani these I did not see for they  didn't ever come  as you're not attempt therefore to  describe them have these however most  wonderful things were related such were  the forces of Endymion their arms were  all alike their helmets were made of  beans for they have beans they're of a  prodigious size and strength and their  scaly breastplates of lupines  sewed together for the sk